From f3a4f5b3fc700cb34fe622ab2d102c1b12bb8ed9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:12:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-120: the toolbox has the IO lamps and panel
 buttons (0.120.0)

WPF's Toolbox lists the project's own controls too. Here it had only the seven VCL ones.
Now MyLedLane / MyLed (IO lamps), ALed (a lamp without an Alias), BtnPanelLane / BtnPanel
(IO panel buttons) as well: the page generator's markup (span.aled with --led-on /
--led-off, div.btnpanel flat with the four --bp-* colours), the sizes and colours the
golden .dfm files use most, BCB6's names (MyLedLane1, BtnPanelLane1 ...), the Alias left
empty for the grid's Alias row (the IO table's names); shape / colours / Style in the
"IO" category (0.119).

Tests: lib 166, smoke 194, panels all pass (lib: 12 templates, each one balanced element,
the IO ones' markup; smoke: the toolbox's 13 rows, MyLedLane1 / BtnPanelLane1 put into
Panel2 as the generator writes them). The real VS Code layer still cannot start: VS Code's
own update (CodeSetup) holds its mutex until VS Code is closed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
